  "worked_solution": "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )=-1$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi )=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =5(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi )) \\\\  & =5(-1+\\text{i}\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
